[SO-74426052] Q: Trigger useEffect with anotherComponents
A: <p>The pattern you want is called a callback function, just like the <code>onClick</code> of a button. You pass a function to your components that get executed given a condition. If you want <code>fetchWines</code> to be called again, then just pass the function in as a prop.</p>
<p>Favorites Component:</p>
<pre><code>&lt;Card listWines={vinosFavs} refresh={fetchWines} /&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Card Component</p>
<pre><code>&lt;BtnFavs onDelete={refresh} ... /&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>BtnFavs Component</p>
<pre><code>onDelete();
</code></pre>
<p>You can name it whatever you want, but generally callbacks will be named like <code>on&lt;condition&gt;</code>.</p>
<hr />
<p>If you really wanted <code>useEffect</code> to be triggered then you would pass a <code>setState</code> function that set one of the dependencies, but I don't see a point in this case.</p>


